  {
   "title": "RENDER TO REALITY",
   "pieces": [
    {
     "type": "text2",
     "left": "<p>The story behind the booths is a long one, dating back to 2019 when the concept was initially pitched. Originally conceptualized for the film premiere in 2020, the COVID pandemic had different ideas, delaying the release of the movie, and ultimately this activation, well over a year. The end result was a build that looked almost identical to the very first pitch.</p>",
     "right": "<p>The build itself was always a hit with the hourglass symbol presented as a daunting 9ft structure that fans could walk into. Reflective walls, intense, pulsating red lighting and a shiny floor created an environment that was truly unique and felt like being in the movie itself. Exterior branding added to the effect, doubling as a secondary photo opp for fans and talent.</p>"
    },
    {
